# Migrating Flat Pulumi Program to ComponentResource with Aliases

## Concept

A flat Pulumi program defines all resources at the stack root level. When migrating to `ComponentResource`, you encapsulate logically related resources into a component class. Without `aliases`, Pulumi treats the new URNs as different resources and will destroy/recreate them. Aliases map old URNs to new ones, preserving state.

## General Migration Pattern

### Before (Flat)

```typescript
const bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket("app-assets", {
  versioningEnabled: true,
  serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: { /* ... */ },
});

const cluster = new aws.eks.Cluster("web-cluster", {
  nodeGroupConfigs: [{ /* ... */ }],
});

const dbInstance = new aws.rds.Instance("postgres-db", {
  allocatedStorage: 50,
  // ...
});
```

### After (ComponentResource)

```typescript
class WebAppInfra extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
  public bucket: aws.s3.Bucket;
  public cluster: aws.eks.Cluster;
  public dbInstance: aws.rds.Instance;

  constructor(name: string, args: WebAppInfraArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
    super("custom:infrastructure:WebAppInfra", name, {}, opts);

    this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`${name}-assets`, {
      versioningEnabled: true,
      serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: { /* ... */ },
    }, { parent: this });

    this.cluster = new aws.eks.Cluster(`${name}-cluster`, {
      nodeGroupConfigs: [{ /* ... */ }],
    }, { parent: this });

    this.dbInstance = new aws.rds.Instance(`${name}-db`, {
      allocatedStorage: 50,
    }, { parent: this });

    this.registerOutputs({});
  }
}
```

## Aliases to Prevent Replacement

Add the `aliases` option to each resource to map its previous flat-program URN. The alias URN follows the pattern:

```
urn:pulumi:<stack>::<project>::<type>::<name>
```

For a resource originally named `"app-assets"` at the stack root, its old URN is:
```
urn:pulumi:dev::my-project::aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::app-assets
```

When moving it into a component named `"web-app"` as a child with logical name `"assets"`, add:

```typescript
this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`${name}-assets`, {
  versioningEnabled: true,
  serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: { /* ... */ },
}, {
  parent: this,
  aliases: [
    { name: "app-assets" },  // Simple: matches the old resource name
  ],
});
```

For explicit URN aliasing (more robust across refactorings):

```typescript
const pulumiConfig = new pulumi.Config();
const stack = pulumi.getStack();
const project = pulumi.getProject();

this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`${name}-assets`, {
  versioningEnabled: true,
  serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: { /* ... */ },
}, {
  parent: this,
  aliases: [
    {
      type: "aws:s3/bucket:Bucket",
      name: "app-assets",
    },
  ],
});
```

## Multi-Stack Example (Dev & Prod)

For the scenario with `dev.yaml` and `prod.yaml` stacks:

```typescript
const config = new pulumi.Config();
const env = config.require("environment"); // "dev" or "prod"

// Environment-specific sizing
const specs = {
  dev: { nodeCount: 2, nodeType: "t3.medium", dbSize: "db.t3.micro" },
  prod: { nodeCount: 4, nodeType: "t3.large", dbSize: "db.t3.medium" },
};

class WebAppInfra extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
  public bucket: aws.s3.Bucket;
  public cluster: aws.eks.Cluster;
  public dbInstance: aws.rds.Instance;
  public iamRole: aws.iam.Role;
  public secret: aws.secretsmanager.Secret;

  constructor(
    name: string,
    args: WebAppInfraArgs,
    opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
  ) {
    super("custom:infrastructure:WebAppInfra", name, {}, opts);

    const spec = specs[env as keyof typeof specs];

    // S3 Bucket
    this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`${name}-assets`, {
      versioningEnabled: true,
      serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: {
        rules: [{
          applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: {
            sseAlgorithm: "AES256",
          },
        }],
      },
      blockPublicAcls: true,
      blockPublicPolicy: true,
      ignorePublicAcls: true,
      restrictPublicBuckets: true,
      ...(env === "prod" && {
        replicationConfiguration: {
          role: /* ARN of replication role */,
          rules: [{
            destination: {
              bucket: /* us-west-2 bucket ARN */,
              replicationTime: { time: 15, unit: "minutes" },
            },
          }],
        },
      }),
    }, {
      parent: this,
      aliases: [{ name: "app-assets" }],
    });

    // EKS Cluster
    this.cluster = new aws.eks.Cluster(`${name}-cluster`, {
      nodeGroupConfigs: [{
        desiredCapacity: spec.nodeCount,
        maxSize: spec.nodeCount + 2,
        minSize: spec.nodeCount,
        instanceType: spec.nodeType,
      }],
    }, {
      parent: this,
      aliases: [{ name: "web-cluster" }],
    });

    // RDS Instance
    this.dbInstance = new aws.rds.Instance(`${name}-db`, {
      allocatedStorage: env === "dev" ? 20 : 100,
      engine: "postgres",
      engineVersion: "14.7",
      instanceClass: spec.dbSize,
      dbName: "appdb",
      skipFinalSnapshot: env === "dev",
      finalSnapshotIdentifier: env === "prod" ? `${name}-final-snapshot` : undefined,
      deletionProtection: env === "prod",
      multiAz: env === "prod",
      storageEncrypted: true,
      publiclyAccessible: false,
      backupRetentionPeriod: env === "prod" ? 30 : 7,
      copyTagsToSnapshot: true,
    }, {
      parent: this,
      aliases: [{ name: "postgres-db" }],
    });

    // IAM Role
    this.iamRole = new aws.iam.Role(`${name}-service-role`, {
      assumeRolePolicy: pulumi.output(aws.iam.getPolicyDocument({
        statements: [{
          actions: ["sts:AssumeRole"],
          principals: [{
            type: "Service",
            identifiers: ["eks.amazonaws.com"],
          }],
        }],
      })).json,
    }, {
      parent: this,
      aliases: [{ name: "service-account-role" }],
    });

    // Attach policy (prod: least-privilege, dev: broader)
    if (env === "prod") {
      new aws.iam.RolePolicyAttachment(`${name}-s3-read-only`, {
        role: this.iamRole,
        policyArn: aws.iam.ManagedPolicies.AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess,
      }, { parent: this });
    } else {
      new aws.iam.RolePolicyAttachment(`${name}-admin`, {
        role: this.iamRole,
        policyArn: aws.iam.ManagedPolicies.AdministratorAccess,
      }, { parent: this });
    }

    // Secrets Manager Secret (encrypted at rest, no plaintext in Git)
    this.secret = new aws.secretsmanager.Secret(`${name}-db-secret`, {
      description: "Database connection string",
      // Value sourced from config, never committed plaintext
      // e.g., pulumi config set --secret db-connection-string "postgres://..."
    }, {
      parent: this,
      aliases: [{ name: "db-connection-secret" }],
    });

    const dbSecretVersion = new aws.secretsmanager.SecretVersion(
      `${name}-db-secret-version`,
      {
        secretId: this.secret.id,
        secretString: config.requireSecret("db-connection-string"),
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    this.registerOutputs({
      bucketName: this.bucket.id,
      clusterEndpoint: this.cluster.endpoint,
      dbEndpoint: this.dbInstance.endpoint,
      secretArn: this.secret.arn,
    });
  }
}

const webApp = new WebAppInfra("web-app", {}, {
  protect: env === "prod", // Prevent accidental deletion in prod
});

export const bucketName = webApp.bucket.id;
export const clusterName = webApp.cluster.name;
```

## Stack Configuration (dev.yaml & prod.yaml)

**dev.yaml:**
```yaml
environment: dev
db-connection-string:
  secure: AAABAxxxxxxxxxxxx...  # `pulumi config set --secret`
```

**prod.yaml:**
```yaml
environment: prod
db-connection-string:
  secure: AAABAyyyyyyyyyyyy...
```

## Deployment Steps

1. **Verify current state:**
   ```
   pulumi stack export > backup.json
   ```

2. **Update code** to add the component and aliases.

3. **Preview migration:**
   ```
   pulumi preview --stack dev
   ```
   Expect to see updates (re-parenting) but **no deletions**.

4. **Apply:**
   ```
   pulumi up --stack dev
   ```

5. **Repeat for prod:**
   ```
   pulumi up --stack prod
   ```

## Verification

After migration:
- All resources retain their original physical IDs (S3 bucket name, RDS endpoint, etc.)
- Stack outputs reference component properties
- No interruption to the running application
- `pulumi stack export` before and after shows the same physical resources with updated URNs

## Notes on Aliases

- **Simple alias** (`{ name: "old-name" }`) works if the old resource was a direct child of the stack root.
- **Type-qualified alias** includes the resource type for explicit matching across provider versions.
- **Multiple aliases** can be listed if the resource was renamed multiple times; Pulumi matches the first applicable one.
- **Parent component** must be specified (via `parent: this`) for aliases to resolve correctly.
- **Secrets** sourced via `pulumi config set --secret` are stored encrypted in the stack state, never in code.

This pattern preserves environment isolation: `dev` and `prod` stacks remain independently deployable, and migrations are deterministic per stack.
